    "intro": "Two functions are inverses when each composition returns the original input on its domain.",
    "facts": [
      "Check both $f(g(x))=x$ and $g(f(x))=x$.",
      "Check the domain of each composition separately.",
      "$\\sqrt{x^2}=|x|$, so $\\sqrt{x^2}=x$ requires $x\\ge0$."
    ],
    "steps": [
      "Substitute one rule into the other",
      "Simplify both compositions",
      "State the allowed inputs"
    ],
